    "body": "## Parent\n\n#172\n\n## What to build\n\nDeliver per-Task retry, Retry all failed links, synchronization at startup, Tasks-open, local-change, five-minute, and Refresh triggers, authentication pause behavior, isolated failures, unlinking, and both linked-Task Trash choices.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Per-Task retry reuses the canonical Task and cannot duplicate a successful remote record.\n- [ ] Retry all targets failed links only and does not silently resolve missing, conflicted, or changed-externally links.\n- [ ] Startup, Tasks-open, local-change, five-minute, and explicit Refresh triggers use one idempotent synchronization path.\n- [ ] Authentication failures pause automatic retry until reconnection; transient failures remain manually and automatically retryable.\n- [ ] One failing link never blocks synchronization of another Task.\n- [ ] Trashing a linked Task asks whether to delete the external record or preserve and unlink it, with external deletion preselected.\n- [ ] External deletion failure remains recoverable in Trash, and permanent local deletion still requires an explicit warning.\n- [ ] `npm run check` is green.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- #176 — Trash, restore, and permanently delete Tasks\n- #186 — Resolve Google content drift and completion conflicts",
